      <version name="1.0.1" author="Eric Avondo" time="2026-08-17T11:03:33Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[Gain reduction measured by the panel: makeup read from the plugin when the panel sits immediately above a chain-ending compressor, instead of estimated; mono-instantiated plugins measured on the left channel only; native reduction reporting always wins over the measured route; measurement ballistics no longer flattened -- both probes now share the track meter's law and a common decay floor at the service's own rate, so attack and release settings show through.]]></changelog>
